// CF-2: `&&` in a guard is a MULTIPLY of the two 0/1 comparisons, and it
// is the LAST link of the chain that is retargeted to the condition
// register - not the comparisons, which write ordinary half-register
// lanes at fp32.
//
// Measured shape: two comparisons into H lanes, then MUL to the CC at
// fx12, then KIL (NE.x).
void main(float4 c : TEXCOORD0, uniform float u_t, out float4 o : COLOR)
{
    if (u_t > 0.0 && c.a < u_t) discard;
    o = c;
}
